{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996322-majesty-and-lashing-out","id":996322,"title":"Majesty and Lashing Out","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-31T16:48:02-07:00","id":996322,"title":"Majesty and Lashing Out","content":"I have a couple of questions regarding the two topics of my title:<br /> <br /> a) Is the first level of Majesty an obvious supernatural effect to other other vampires? Do other vampires know they are being affected by a supernatural power, or do people mostly assume the Daeva is that magnetic?<br /> <br /> b) If the answer for the question above is that it isn't an obvious effect, how does Lashing Out work? Does your Beast do it automatically? How can you Lash Out on an effect you don't know is supernatural?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T17:14:00-07:00","id":996329,"title":"","content":"That's a complicated question. I would say it's not immediately obvious until the power is turned directly against you.<br /> <br /> Yes awe technically effects everyone in range. I would say if there was a reason to roll wits composure - their majesty dots for anything revolving around your own safety you could choose to lash out to break their hold on your attention. <br /> <br /> If the vampire attempted to draw you to them you could lash out as well. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking this is more a subconscious defense but the player still gets to decide if they do it.<br /> <br /> For any other use of majesty I wouldn't want to take away player agency but if they are using awe just to get you to be more polite as opposed to making a request I don't know. I would likely have the situation role played out first and then dice rolls as needed. <br /> <br /> Of course any lash out attempt would still require a willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T17:48:17-07:00","id":996359,"title":"","content":"FAQ: <br /> Does a vampire affected by Majesty 1, Awe, know that they\u2019re being affected by a supernatural power?<br /> Not automatically. They just feel what Awe wants them to feel. However, they retain their faculties enough that if a Daeva seems too amazing to be true, they might be able to turn around and defy it with the predatory aura.<br /> <br /> Majesty has always been super subtle. You would have to have a good reason to think they are using the power because if you are wrong, you just attacked them - they know it. <br /> <br /> Lashing out is noticeable. And it is something a vampire needs to choose to do. It is not something that goes without repercussions.<br /> <br /> Lashing out requires you to roll 1 of 3 attributes + BP against theirs. So if they are using awe and you lash out and lose, you are now affected by awe and a condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 10-31-2016, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T20:01:26-07:00","id":996407,"title":"","content":"Actually can you expand this topic to also include Nightmare? They're similar and also have a lashing out component.<br /> <br /> Lashing out of dread presence allows the vamp to apply his willpower again against him. How obvious is dread presence? more or less obvious to awe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T20:36:17-07:00","id":996417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996322-majesty-and-lashing-out?p=996407#post996407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually can you expand this topic to also include Nightmare? They're similar and also have a lashing out component.<br /> <br /> Lashing out of dread presence allows the vamp to apply his willpower again against him. How obvious is dread presence? more or less obvious to awe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a bit more obvious. Awe may make someone uncannily attractive, but Dread Presence can turn your chow mein into worms. When that happens it's clear <i>something</i> supernatural is going on, and the description does make it clear that you register the user as the source of your fear, even if only on a subconscious level. If they leave it at just a creepy vibe and don't make you hallucinate though (or only make other people hallucinate), it's about as subtle as Awe (to you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T06:18:15-07:00","id":996548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996322-majesty-and-lashing-out?p=996417#post996417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably a bit more obvious. Awe may make someone uncannily attractive, but Dread Presence can turn your chow mein into worms. When that happens it's clear <i>something</i> supernatural is going on, and the description does make it clear that you register the user as the source of your fear, even if only on a subconscious level. If they leave it at just a creepy vibe and don't make you hallucinate though (or only make other people hallucinate), it's about as subtle as Awe (to you).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this here, if you make it just the creepy vibe, then it's super subtle. <br /> I always took the hallucinations to be more like just super brief moments. If I looked down into my food and saw a maggots, looked away, looked back and didnt see anything. I probably wouldn't jump to Nightmare, or Ghosts, because they arent suppose to exist... right? Perhaps I was just crazy?<br /> Though if you did do it on a vampire who knows what Nightmare is, I would definitely give them some sort of roll to realize that's what just happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T06:26:13-07:00","id":996551,"title":"","content":"About dread presence (and sorry for the off topic), can someone use it while he's obfuscated? For example, creating illusion with the 4th power and lashing dread presence to extend the illusion to everyone in the place, could be possible staying invisible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T06:54:40-07:00","id":996559,"title":"","content":"Back to Awe. For me, you can guess it's being used on you if you know the vampire and had interactions with her while she wasn't using Majesty because then, when she turns it on, you can pick up on the fact you are feeling differently. I would even say that if the vampire turns Majesty on as you are having an interaction, you may pick up on it because of the sudden change, it doesn't matter how subtle the power is supposed to be. This is why Awe is especially effective against mortals but more limited or at least risky against vampire you regularly have interactions with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12610-lestat","name":"Lestat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12610_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:33:14-07:00","id":996575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996322-majesty-and-lashing-out?p=996551#post996551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About dread presence (and sorry for the off topic), can someone use it while he's obfuscated? For example, creating illusion with the 4th power and lashing dread presence to extend the illusion to everyone in the place, could be possible staying invisible?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> forgive me I might not be answering correctly because I am not sure your question. Lashing out is one, thing But I am assuming you dont mean that, but more of letting out dread presence. I don't think that you can send your beast out while also drawing your beast in with obfuscate. Though I dont think it would be out of the scope of reality to make something like that a devotion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lestat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996322-majesty-and-lashing-out?p=996559#post996559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to Awe. For me, you can guess it's being used on you if you know the vampire and had interactions with her while she wasn't using Majesty because then, when she turns it on, you can pick up on the fact you are feeling differently. I would even say that if the vampire turns Majesty on as you are having an interaction, you may pick up on it because of the sudden change, it doesn't matter how subtle the power is supposed to be. This is why Awe is especially effective against mortals but more limited or at least risky against vampire you regularly have interactions with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will give you that, if you are known for using Majesty a lot and the people you talk to are aware you do it, they might be able to sense exactly when you use it.<br /> <br /> But say you are at a party, chatting it up, socializing. the vampire is a few feet away. you look over beccause their laughter rings out, and notice them. Maybe you even want to go talk to them now. You know they would like that. Your eyes meet for a just a moment and you just melt. Which stage of that did the vampire turn on awe? Did the vampire even turn on awe? we all randomly or suddenly get drawn to some sort of sound or visual cue. some word in a conversation draws your attention. Is it magic or nature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 11-01-2016, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:34:28-07:00","id":996577,"title":"","content":"Considering the fact that the clanbook has a human describing how he can identify the vampire in the room simply by noting who everyone else is paying attention to, I'd say it's use is neither subtle nor undetectable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:57:58-07:00","id":996589,"title":"","content":"You could certainly play it that way. However, do keep in mind that the Clan books are 1E. No one said it was undetectable, everyone ( even the FAQ ) said you would need a reason. Even if that reason is &quot;too good to be true&quot; It isn't like a light switch flicked on or like Protean 3 when people KNOW you did it. Just about every Majesty 2E thread in this place says to the effect it is Subtle.<br /> <br /> I know nothing of this clan book or the human within it, but considering that this human can just point out a &gt; vampire &lt; in the room just like that, this human is probably a special case.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/67072-how-subtle-are-dominate-and-majesty-now\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...nd-majesty-now</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/167874-lashing-out-and-awe\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ng-out-and-awe</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815332-2ed-idol\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...15332-2ed-idol</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-about-majesty</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines\"> B&amp;S 'Lashing Out' against Disciplines. - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Majesty1 (Awe) and Nightmare1 (Dread Presence) both have no activation roll, no cost, and state that the only way for Kindred to resist is by 'Lashing Out' and reference the Lashing Out page. However, that section does not at all comment upon using 'Lashing Out' in this fashion. So how precisely does this </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> From Rose: <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> [COLOR=#6A6A6A !important]<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">12-27-2013, 04:04 PM</span></span>[/COLOR]<br /> </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>Charlaquin</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37484#post37484\">View Post</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Personally, I think its realistic hazard of using mind-affecting powers that target large groups of people. You shouldn't be able to just turn on your love beams in a crowded room and expect no one to push back. And I don't think its reasonable to say &quot;well I'm only trying to impress the people who won't mind it&quot;. But that's just my personal taste, I like discipline use to always be a calculated risk. If that's not your bag, by all means allow it.</span><br /> </span><br /> </i></span><br /> </span><br /> That was my original intent with the power, and the way I ran it in playtest,* but I don't see a problem with &quot;targeted Awe.&quot;<br /> <br /> But it also seems like a reasonable thing to change (as you say, personal taste), and I can sort of see a Prince going &quot;well, I only want this one to play for the plebes&quot; and the Blood backing that up.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>Charlaquin</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37660#post37660\">View Post</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Only for that one guy who Lashed Out though, everyone else is still affected, or so I thought.</span><br /> </span><br /> </i></span><br /> </span><br /> That's correct. Awe isn't an enchantment that just shatters if one person resists. If you lose a PA contest, you might be publicly humiliated, but you still look great.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>Unahim</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37801#post37801\">View Post</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">That also implies Majesty is directly noticeable, though, which I've always assumed it wasn't.</span><br /> </span><br /> </i></span><br /> </span><br /> It isn't, and I'll put that in the FAQ. However, people retain enough faculties to go &quot;Martin looks smooth as silk and cool as air. Martin's a schlub. Since I know he's a Daeva and they can fuck with my head, maybe I ought to get in his face and make him back off whatever he's doing to me.&quot;<br /> <br /> * Which did in fact feature a predatory aura contest after someone injudiciously charmed a whole room.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 11-01-2016, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T08:30:53-07:00","id":996613,"title":"","content":"It's probably a case of &quot;I know there's a daeva in this room. It's probably the dude everyone is fawning over.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T09:50:09-07:00","id":996659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996322-majesty-and-lashing-out?p=996575#post996575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> forgive me I might not be answering correctly because I am not sure your question. Lashing out is one, thing But I am assuming you dont mean that, but more of letting out dread presence. I don't think that you can send your beast out while also drawing your beast in with obfuscate. Though I dont think it would be out of the scope of reality to make something like that a devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes sorry, I used the wrong word. I meant just to use dread presence not lashing out the beast. <br /> <br /> My question was: is posssible to use dread presence during obfuscate, in order to create mass illusions or a frightening atmosphere without revealing your presence? Or should it be possible just with a devotion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T10:25:47-07:00","id":996674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996322-majesty-and-lashing-out?p=996659#post996659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes sorry, I used the wrong word. I meant just to use dread presence not lashing out the beast.<br /> <br /> My question was: is posssible to use dread presence during obfuscate, in order to create mass illusions or a frightening atmosphere without revealing your presence? Or should it be possible just with a devotion?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I stated before, I think a Devotion would be appropriate as I don't believe you can, by RAW, hide (obfuscate ) and be noticed (nightmare's effects ) at the same time. I base this on the Devotion Wet Dream where it says you cant use awe and dread presence at the same time. Though I am not 100% sure on this.<br /> <br /> Perhaps your Devotion could be called something like : Hidden Nightmares<br /> Obfuscate 3 + Nightmare 2<br /> This devotion would allow you to use the effects of Nightmare while continuing to stay invisible with Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T11:24:12-07:00","id":996708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will give you that, if you are known for using Majesty a lot and the people you talk to are aware you do it, they might be able to sense exactly when you use it.<br /> <br /> But say you are at a party, chatting it up, socializing. the vampire is a few feet away. you look over beccause their laughter rings out, and notice them. Maybe you even want to go talk to them now. You know they would like that. Your eyes meet for a just a moment and you just melt. Which stage of that did the vampire turn on awe? Did the vampire even turn on awe? we all randomly or suddenly get drawn to some sort of sound or visual cue. some word in a conversation draws your attention. Is it magic or nature? </div> </div> </div>Like I said, it depends on how well you know the vampire using it or how many interactions you have had with her. I know it is supposed to be a subtle power, but when I read the description, I see it as a supernatural charisma magnifier. If it felt just like a &quot;natural charisma increase&quot;, the power would not be as powerful as it is. It clearly says you could beat someone up and still look cool to people. In the real world, you could be the most charismatic people, you would not have people in awe of you if you just had beaten up someone to a pulp before. So it takes something supernatural and powerful to drive that effect, and to me, it's also what makes this power interesting.<br /> <br /> Now, that being said, I do agree it depends on context and in your example, it can definitely work against a vampire who knows you a bit. I just think you have to be a bit more conservative in HOW you use it on vampires who know you well. That's my interpretation of it, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12610-lestat","name":"Lestat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12610_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T12:33:17-07:00","id":996756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996322-majesty-and-lashing-out?p=996674#post996674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As I stated before, I think a Devotion would be appropriate as I don't believe you can, by RAW, hide (obfuscate ) and be noticed (nightmare's effects ) at the same time. I base this on the Devotion Wet Dream where it says you cant use awe and dread presence at the same time. Though I am not 100% sure on this.<br /> <br /> Perhaps your Devotion could be called something like : Hidden Nightmares<br /> Obfuscate 3 + Nightmare 2<br /> This devotion would allow you to use the effects of Nightmare while continuing to stay invisible with Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds more or less like Wraith's Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:16:13-07:00","id":996797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996322-majesty-and-lashing-out?p=996756#post996756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds more or less like Wraith's Presence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ha! It really does! I was super close to the requirements too. I dont take either of those two disciplines too much which is why it didnt jump out at me as already existing! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T01:25:09-07:00","id":997045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996322-majesty-and-lashing-out?p=996575#post996575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will give you that, if you are known for using Majesty a lot and the people you talk to are aware you do it, they might be able to sense exactly when you use it.<br /> <br /> But say you are at a party, chatting it up, socializing. the vampire is a few feet away. you look over beccause their laughter rings out, and notice them. Maybe you even want to go talk to them now. You know they would like that. Your eyes meet for a just a moment and you just melt. Which stage of that did the vampire turn on awe? Did the vampire even turn on awe? we all randomly or suddenly get drawn to some sort of sound or visual cue. some word in a conversation draws your attention. Is it magic or nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. It's not uncommon to ignore somebody and suddenly become more attracted to them out of the blue, either. Sometimes you meet someone again and it feels different, better than their first impression. It's not mystical, although people do notice the shift in emotion - having feelings for somebody you never thought you'd consider is common albeit still surprising (&quot;you seem different now -- that's a good thing&quot;, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}